@bruvzg Testing with  jp106 keyboard showed no issues.
With the BÉPO keyboard layout, since the 'U' key is located in the position of the physical 'S' key, it seems natural that the 'U' key would be input. However, I'm not familiar with French keyboards, so I support this PR.
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/B%C3%89PO

@bruvzg Thank you. I understand now.
The user is using a BÉPO physical keyboard, where normal input produces a 'U' key, but when pressed with Ctrl, the OS reports it as an 'S' key.
The problem occurs when this is overwritten by the Unicode value 'U' that was reported.
